So, here we go.
I bought Black Desert Online for the 2nd time some days ago, first time I bought it and refunded it because of the lack of v-sync option and my frame rates were dipping pretty hard as the GPU usage was very low, I fixed it eventually the second time by paying a visit to the trusty nVidia control panel and making a profile for the game with the v-sync forced off and the game fullscreen.
I don't have a lot of time in-game but as a big MMO vet I can do something like pros and cons from what I've seen of BDO so far:
Pros:
- Game's beautiful, good graphics and theme, for sure the most visually appealing MMO experience I ever had so far;
- Good story line so far, and the Black Spirit is such a character..;
- Combat, combat, combat! So fluid and engaging, I feel like I'm playing Devil May Cry but on a MMO, thumbs up Kakao!;~
- The mobility system is awesome aswell, you don't have only to run around, you can actually use combos to move around quickly in or out of combat;
- SO, but, SO much stuff to do, it's overwhelming at the start (and still is 6 hours in) but eventually you'll get the hang of it while questing;
- Lots of nice details in the convos you can have with various npcs, the animity system for example, even the AFK fishing thing and lots more;
- The family system is so cool, you can actually maintain a healthy bunch of alts and it will help your main, shared stuff between your family characters, etc;
Cons:
- Still to find a big con worth of mentioning but it seems the game is a bit on the grindy side, but no problem as the combat is so engaging;
I will update this review when I have more hours in, but so far, so good!
Cheers!

